cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use dehype, its scoring method or its data snapshots, please cite it as below."
title: "dehype: a daily AI reality briefing and evidence-weighted tracker of AI research papers, repositories and hype"
abstract: >-
  dehype publishes a daily briefing of what happened in AI in the last 24 hours, with each story's evidence and verdict state, in
  English and Portuguese, on a ledger anyone can verify. It also ranks AI research papers and GitHub repositories on agents, harnesses and context layers, JEPA,
  JEV (decision models) and world/action models, and compares sampled attention (Hype) with evidence
  of substance (Real) across the wider AI world. Scores are confidence-aware: missing evidence shrinks
  a score toward the median instead of being filled in.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Felipe
    family-names: Rosa
    affiliation: Namastex
  - name: Namastex
repository-code: "https://github.com/namastex888/dehype"
url: "https://namastex888.github.io/dehype/"
# Code is AGPL-3.0-only from the commit that replaced the MIT LICENSE; the data (web/*.json, feeds, ledger) are CC BY-SA 4.0 for our
# selection, arrangement and computed fields only. Earlier commits and the 2.0 release (2026-10-07, the last one under MIT and CC BY 4.0)
# keep MIT and CC BY 4.0; no version is named here until the next release is cut.
license:
  - AGPL-3.0-only
  - CC-BY-SA-4.0
keywords:
  - AI agents
  - context engineering
  - JEPA
  - world models
  - research trends
  - open research
